---
// Accessibility statement. Keep the "tested" and "pending" lists in step with
// docs/a11y-testing.md; do not claim more than that record shows.
const reviewed = "9 November 2026";
const issues = "https://github.com/Bananajunk/portfolio/issues";
const link =
  "inline-flex min-h-11 items-center text-accent underline underline-offset-4";
---

<section
  id="accessibility"
  aria-labelledby="accessibility-heading"
  class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6 py-16"
  data-testid="accessibility-statement"
>
  <h2
    id="accessibility-heading"
    class="font-display text-step-2 font-medium leading-tight tracking-tight"
  >
    Accessibility statement
  </h2>
  <p class="mt-5 max-w-prose text-step-0 text-ink-soft">
    This Site aims to conform to WCAG 2.2 level AA. It has not been independently
    audited, so this is a goal and not a claim of full conformance. Last
    reviewed {reviewed}.
  </p>

  <h3 class="mt-10 font-display text-step-1 font-medium leading-tight">
    What was tested and how
  </h3>
  <ul class="mt-4 max-w-prose list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-step-0 text-ink-soft">
    <li>
      Automated checks with axe-core on every build, in all three Time of day
      themes with Calm mode on and off.
    </li>
    <li>
      Keyboard-only use in Chromium: tab order, visible focus, a skip link, no
      keyboard traps and focus not hidden behind the sticky navigation.
    </li>
    <li>
      Reflow at 200% and 400% zoom (a 320 CSS pixel wide window), with no
      horizontal scrolling.
    </li>
    <li>
      Forced colours mode, reduced motion and Calm mode, and touch target size
      (at least 24 by 24 CSS pixels, aiming for 44).
    </li>
    <li>
      The sticker board can be used without dragging: select a sticker, then use
      the arrow buttons, arrow keys or click a spot.
    </li>
    <li>Text and interface colour contrast, checked on every build.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3 class="mt-10 font-display text-step-1 font-medium leading-tight">
    Known limitations and pending checks
  </h3>
  <ul class="mt-4 max-w-prose list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-step-0 text-ink-soft">
    <li>
      Tested with VoiceOver in Safari on macOS before launch, with no problems
      reported. VoiceOver on iOS has not been tested yet.
    </li>
    <li>
      Not yet tested on real touch devices or with browsers other than Chromium
      beyond the checks above.
    </li>
    <li>
      Automated and scripted checks catch only part of WCAG 2.2, so there may be
      issues they do not find.
    </li>
    <li>
      The Resume PDF download has not been checked with assistive technology.
      The same facts are on this page as text.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3 class="mt-10 font-display text-step-1 font-medium leading-tight">
    Report a problem
  </h3>
  <p class="mt-4 max-w-prose text-step-0 text-ink-soft">
    If something here is hard to use, tell me and I will aim to reply within a
    few business days. Email{" "}
    <a class={link} href="mailto:cl2reid@gmail.com">cl2reid@gmail.com</a>
    or{" "}
    <a class={link} href={issues}>open an issue on GitHub</a>.
  </p>
</section>
